<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Templated from VFEP's VFEP_WarcasketHelmet_Controller (VFEP v4.03,
    1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Headgear.xml); fields not discussed here, uiIconScale and
    the psychic and toxic offsets included, are the Controller's, its drone module left off.
    Plating, tags and the market-value references follow the armor's header.

    Tuning, first pass: ComponentSpacer 4 / Plasteel 60, the Controller's and Brute's price for a
    helmet with a function of its own; whether the command range below prices like one, or a
    mechlink passive (bandwidth or control groups) joins it, is the tuning pass's question, in
    TODOs.md.

    Command range (the CommandRangeExtension entry, Source/1.6/CommandRange/): a mechanitor
    wearing the helmet may order their drafted mechs anywhere on the map they share (scope
    CurrentMap), where vanilla stops every move and attack order at 24.9 cells from the overseer.
    The helmet carries it as the set's command visor, the piece the lore gives the pilot's
    mechlink; the mod settings may move the entry to the shoulders, widen it to every mechanitor
    or switch it off, and override the scope (Anywhere drops the same-map rule too; Radius keeps
    vanilla's shape at the radius below) and the radius, which is the Radius scope's reach and
    the settings slider's default, left at vanilla's 24.9 so switching to that scope starts from
    vanilla. The settings write every choice back onto this entry at startup and when the window
    closes; CommandRange's header has the vanilla call paths and the rules.

    Art: the helmet alone of the three pieces ships masks (_northm/_eastm/_southm for the worn
    graphic, _m for the item icon), so it draws with CutoutComplex and useWornGraphicMask, as
    VFEP's Controller helmet does and as vanilla's prestige armors are the pattern: the
    CompColorable colour paints the mask's red areas and the black-masked trim keeps its painted
    colour (apparel graphics pass white as colorTwo). Mask names differ by graphic class:
    Graphic_Multi reads <path>_northm, Graphic_Single <path>_m.

    ApparelExtension priority 1, for the reason in the armor def's header: the
    VFEP_WarcasketHelmetBase parent carries its own, and only the highest-priority copy keeps
    its fields whole (Merge still ORs the parent's isUnifiedApparel and hideHead in). Any new
    ApparelExtension field for this piece goes on this entry.

    Compat: SOS2Patch.xml gives it the EVA tag and Insulation_Cold 100 alongside the armor;
    the VGE vacuum patch lowers its VacuumResistance to VGE1's warcasket-helmet value; the
    1.6/Mods/CombatExtended/Patches/ root rescales its plating and seals it against CE's
    smoke, which reads no tox immunity.
  -->
  <VFEPirates.WarcasketDef ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketHelmetBase">
    <defName>OLWC_WarcasketHelmet_Overlord</defName>
    <label>overlord warcasket helmet</label>
    <shortDescription>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket helmet with standard protection, equipped with a command visor for the pilot's mechlink.</shortDescription>
    <description>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket helmet with standard protection, equipped with a command visor for the pilot's mechlink.\n\nA 10th-generation design from the government program that rebuilt captured pirate rigs around its own power armor and gave them to veterans who could no longer serve any other way. The Overlord was its rig for veteran mechanitors, who would command their own mechs in the field rather than join a squad.\n\nThe Overlord series is meant for a mechanitor who goes into battle alone, with only their mechs beside them. The core in the shell holds only a few charges and recharges very slowly, so they are best saved for the mechs that matter most. The shoulders and helmet carry processors that support the pilot's mechlink, and the arms are left free for smithing and hacking. Because the plating is far tougher than a mechanitor's usual armor, the pilot can lead from the front line rather than from behind the mechs.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketOverlord/WarcasketOverlordHelmet</texPath>
      <shaderType>CutoutComplex</shaderType>
    </graphicData>
    <uiIconScale>1.25</uiIconScale>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>8</Mass>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>2</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>1</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>1</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>10</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>10</Insulation_Heat>
      <EquipDelay>1</EquipDelay>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <PsychicSensitivity>-0.5</PsychicSensitivity>
      <ToxicResistance>0.5</ToxicResistance>
      <SlaveSuppressionOffset MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">0.1</SlaveSuppressionOffset>
      <VacuumResistance MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0.7</VacuumResistance>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <costList>
      <ComponentSpacer>4</ComponentSpacer>
      <Plasteel>60</Plasteel>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>FullHead</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketOverlord/WarcasketOverlordHelmet</wornGraphicPath>
      <useWornGraphicMask>true</useWornGraphicMask>
      <layers>
        <li>Overhead</li>
      </layers>
      <tags>
        <li>WarcasketVeteran</li>
        <li>WarcasketAll</li>
      </tags>
    </apparel>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.ApparelExtension">
        <priority>1</priority>
      </li>
      <li Class="OverlordWarcasket.CommandRangeExtension">
        <scope>CurrentMap</scope>
        <radius>24.9</radius>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VFEPirates.WarcasketDef>
</Defs>
